{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the least possible value of the sum \\( S = |x - 1| + |x - 1.5| + |x - 2| \\), we need to consider the behavior of the absolute value function. The expression \\( S \\) is the sum of the distances from \\( x \\) to the points 1, 1.5, and 2 on the number line.\n\nThe optimal value of \\( x \\) that minimizes \\( S \\) is the median of the points 1, 1.5, and 2. This is because the median minimizes the sum of the absolute deviations. In this case, the median is 1.5.\n\nLet's verify this by evaluating \\( S \\) at \\( x = 1.5 \\):\n\\[\nS = |1.5 - 1| + |1.5 - 1.5| + |1.5 - 2| = 0.5 + 0 + 0.5 = 1.\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":591,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,3245,3204,897,315,279,2629,17767,328,284,760,87,481,220,16,91,488,760,87,481,220,16,13,20,91,488,760,87,481,220,17,91,1124,701,582,1184,311,2908,279,7709,315,279,10740,897,729,13,576,7493,17767,328,1124,8,374,279,2629,315,279,26552,504,17767,856,1124,8,311,279,3501,220,16,11,220,16,13,20,11,323,220,17,389,279,1372,1555,382,785,22823,897,315,17767,856,1124,8,429,21187,4756,17767,328,1124,8,374,279,22553,315,279,3501,220,16,11,220,16,13,20,11,323,220,17,13,1096,374,1576,279,22553,21187,4756,279,2629,315,279,10740,85265,13,758,419,1142,11,279,22553,374,220,16,13,20,382,10061,594,10146,419,553,37563,17767,328,1124,8,518,17767,856,284,220,16,13,20,1124,982,59,9640,50,284,760,16,13,20,481,220,16,91,488,760,16,13,20,481,220,16,13,20,91,488,760,16,13,20,481,220,17,91,284,220,15,13,20,488,220,15,488,220,15,13,20,284,220,16,624,59,2533,1249,5978,429,220,16,13,20,374,12824,279,8028,11,582,646,1779,279,2750,315,17767,328,1124,8,518,279,3501,220,16,323,220,17,510,59,9640,59,1318,90,4498,335,856,284,220,16,11,1124,31610,328,284,760,16,481,220,16,91,488,760,16,481,220,16,13,20,91,488,760,16,481,220,17,91,284,220,15,488,220,15,13,20,488,220,16,284,220,16,13