5 + 0 + 0.5 = 1.\n\\]\n\nTo ensure that 1.5 is indeed the minimum, we can check the values of \\( S \\) at the points 1 and 2:\n\\[\n\\text{When } x = 1, \\quad S = |1 - 1| + |1 - 1.5| + |1 - 2| = 0 + 0.5 + 1 = 1.5,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{When } x = 2, \\quad S = |2 - 1| + |2 - 1.5| + |2 - 2| = 1 + 0.5 + 0 = 1.5.\n\\]\n\nSince \\( S = 1 \\) when \\( x = 1.5 \\) and \\( S = 1.5 \\) when \\( x = 1 \\) or \\( x = 2 \\), the minimum value of \\( S \\) is indeed 1.\n\nTherefore, the least possible value of the sum \\( |x - 1| + |x - 1.5| + |x - 2| \\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:225"}
